1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:03,341
Scatterplot questions
look like data analysis,

2
00:00:03,361 --> 00:00:06,091
but many of them come down to one idea.

3
00:00:06,111 --> 00:00:08,769
The line of best fit gives predictions.

4
00:00:08,789 --> 00:00:11,397
The dots show what actually happened.

5
00:00:11,445 --> 00:00:14,817
In this lesson: associations,
reading a line of best fit,

6
00:00:14,837 --> 00:00:19,674
predicted versus actual values,
linear versus exponential models,

7
00:00:19,694 --> 00:00:22,052
and when a prediction can't be trusted.

8
00:00:22,695 --> 00:00:26,530
Then six practice questions,
all with made-up data.

9
00:00:26,550 --> 00:00:29,601
The biggest mistake is
treating the model as exact.

10
00:00:29,621 --> 00:00:31,514
The line describes a trend.

11
00:00:31,693 --> 00:00:34,943
It doesn't promise anything
about any single point.

12
00:00:35,008 --> 00:00:36,773
Start with the cloud of points.

13
00:00:36,793 --> 00:00:40,916
If y tends to go up as x goes up,
that's a positive association.

14
00:00:40,936 --> 00:00:43,165
If y tends to go down, it's negative.

15
00:00:43,185 --> 00:00:46,257
If there's no clear trend,
there's no association.

16
00:00:46,343 --> 00:00:48,021
Notice the word tends.

17
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:50,950
Real data has points
that break the pattern.

18
00:00:51,128 --> 00:00:54,180
So when an answer choice
says always or every,

19
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:55,750
test it against the dots.

20
00:00:55,770 --> 00:00:58,072
And if the points follow a straight path,

21
00:00:58,092 --> 00:01:00,000
the association is linear.

22
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:02,093
If they bend, it's nonlinear.

23
00:01:02,135 --> 00:01:04,508
A line of best fit follows the trend.

24
00:01:04,528 --> 00:01:05,706
Here's one.

25
00:01:05,778 --> 00:01:08,901
The scatterplot shows
the age, x, in years,

26
00:01:08,921 --> 00:01:12,563
and the price, y, in
dollars, of eight used bikes.

27
00:01:12,707 --> 00:01:16,864
The line of best fit is y equals
negative forty x plus four hundred.

28
00:01:16,884 --> 00:01:22,026
The slope is the predicted change
in y for each increase of one in x.

29
00:01:22,205 --> 00:01:24,506
Here, for each additional year of age,

30
00:01:24,526 --> 00:01:27,113
the predicted price
drops by forty dollars.

31
00:01:27,133 --> 00:01:31,161
Keep that order: per one
unit of x, the change in y.

32
00:01:31,181 --> 00:01:35,125
The y intercept is the
predicted y when x is zero.

33
00:01:35,145 --> 00:01:38,125
Here, that's the predicted
price of a brand new bike:

34
00:01:38,145 --> 00:01:39,609
four hundred dollars.

35
00:01:39,824 --> 00:01:42,359
And always say predicted.

36
00:01:42,538 --> 00:01:46,895
The line gives estimates,
not facts about any one bike.

37
00:01:46,945 --> 00:01:48,854
Every point has two y values.

38
00:01:48,874 --> 00:01:50,961
The actual value is where the dot is.

39
00:01:50,981 --> 00:01:54,302
The predicted value is
where the line is at that x.

40
00:01:55,052 --> 00:01:59,837
Take the five-year-old bike that
sold for two hundred thirty dollars.

41
00:01:59,863 --> 00:02:02,413
The line predicts
negative forty times five,

42
00:02:02,433 --> 00:02:04,628
plus four hundred, which is two hundred.

43
00:02:04,648 --> 00:02:07,934
So actual minus predicted
is positive thirty.

44
00:02:08,005 --> 00:02:11,307
A dot above the line is
higher than predicted.

45
00:02:11,327 --> 00:02:13,588
A dot below the line is lower.

46
00:02:13,608 --> 00:02:16,016
Not every scatterplot is a straight line.

47
00:02:16,036 --> 00:02:19,159
If the points curve upward,
getting steeper and steeper,

48
00:02:19,179 --> 00:02:22,848
an exponential model usually
fits better than a line.

49
00:02:22,868 --> 00:02:24,726
In a table, check the pattern.

50
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:27,884
If y goes up by about the
same amount each step,

51
00:02:27,904 --> 00:02:28,976
think linear.

52
00:02:29,118 --> 00:02:32,098
If y gets multiplied by about
the same number each step,

53
00:02:32,118 --> 00:02:33,404
think exponential.

54
00:02:33,436 --> 00:02:37,059
Predicting inside the range of
the data is called interpolation,

55
00:02:37,079 --> 00:02:38,523
and it's usually reasonable.

56
00:02:38,543 --> 00:02:41,309
Predicting outside the
range is extrapolation.

57
00:02:41,329 --> 00:02:43,829
The farther you go, the riskier it gets.

58
00:02:43,921 --> 00:02:46,777
Our bike data covers
ages one through eight.

59
00:02:46,956 --> 00:02:48,937
Ask the line about a
fifteen-year-old bike,

60
00:02:48,957 --> 00:02:52,150
and it predicts a price of
negative two hundred dollars.

61
00:02:52,170 --> 00:02:55,091
The line doesn't know
the trend has to stop.

62
00:02:55,111 --> 00:02:58,018
On the SAT, this topic
shows up in a few ways.

63
00:02:58,038 --> 00:02:59,825
Describe the association.

64
00:02:59,861 --> 00:03:02,055
Interpret a slope or intercept.

65
00:03:02,075 --> 00:03:04,733
Compare predicted and actual values.

66
00:03:04,753 --> 00:03:05,769
Choose a model.

67
00:03:05,789 --> 00:03:08,233
Or decide which statement
the data supports.

68
00:03:08,253 --> 00:03:09,753
We'll do all five.

69
00:03:09,806 --> 00:03:10,679
Question one.

70
00:03:10,699 --> 00:03:12,929
The scatterplot shows the number of hours,

71
00:03:12,949 --> 00:03:17,179
x, that each of ten phones had been
used since its last full charge,

72
00:03:17,199 --> 00:03:19,143
and the phone's remaining battery charge,

73
00:03:19,163 --> 00:03:20,663
y, as a percent.

74
00:03:20,699 --> 00:03:24,913
Which statement best describes
the association between x and y?

75
00:03:24,935 --> 00:03:26,150
Pause and try it.

76
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:31,986
The dots fall from upper
left to lower right.

77
00:03:32,006 --> 00:03:35,487
So as x increases, y tends to decrease.

78
00:03:35,507 --> 00:03:37,308
That's a negative association.

79
00:03:37,328 --> 00:03:38,720
The answer is B.

80
00:03:38,753 --> 00:03:42,323
C is the trap, because
of one word: always.

81
00:03:42,574 --> 00:03:45,268
Look at the phones used
six and seven hours.

82
00:03:45,288 --> 00:03:47,554
The one used longer has more charge left,

83
00:03:47,574 --> 00:03:49,554
sixty percent versus fifty-eight.

84
00:03:49,574 --> 00:03:51,911
So y doesn't always decrease.

85
00:03:51,931 --> 00:03:54,431
The data shows a trend, not a rule.

86
00:03:54,462 --> 00:03:55,514
Question two.

87
00:03:55,534 --> 00:03:58,550
The scatterplot shows the
length, x, in centimeters,

88
00:03:58,570 --> 00:04:02,570
and the mass, y, in grams, of
twelve fish of one species.

89
00:04:02,605 --> 00:04:06,764
The line of best fit is y equals
twenty-five x minus four hundred.

90
00:04:06,784 --> 00:04:11,226
Which choice is the best interpretation
of twenty-five in this context?

91
00:04:11,246 --> 00:04:12,460
Pause and try it.

92
00:04:15,710 --> 00:04:20,619
Twenty-five is the slope, and
its units are y units per x unit:

93
00:04:20,639 --> 00:04:22,103
grams per centimeter.

94
00:04:22,246 --> 00:04:25,262
So for each increase of
one centimeter in length,

95
00:04:25,282 --> 00:04:28,475
the predicted mass increases
by twenty-five grams.

96
00:04:28,495 --> 00:04:30,210
The answer is C.

97
00:04:30,266 --> 00:04:33,068
A flips it around, from
grams to centimeters.

98
00:04:33,088 --> 00:04:35,123
That's reading the slope backwards.

99
00:04:35,159 --> 00:04:36,532
D swaps the numbers.

100
00:04:36,552 --> 00:04:40,175
And B describes the y intercept,
which is negative four hundred,

101
00:04:40,195 --> 00:04:41,552
not twenty-five.

102
00:04:41,710 --> 00:04:43,888
That intercept is worth a look.

103
00:04:44,067 --> 00:04:47,638
Negative four hundred grams
for a fish with no length?

104
00:04:47,817 --> 00:04:52,225
It's meaningless, because zero
centimeters is far outside the data,

105
00:04:52,245 --> 00:04:54,474
which runs from twenty to forty.

106
00:04:54,494 --> 00:04:56,991
Not every intercept has a real meaning.

107
00:04:57,011 --> 00:04:58,098
Question three.

108
00:04:58,118 --> 00:05:00,347
The scatterplot shows
the high temperature,

109
00:05:00,367 --> 00:05:03,348
x, in degrees Fahrenheit,
and the number of hot drinks,

110
00:05:03,368 --> 00:05:06,455
y, sold at a coffee cart on twelve days.

111
00:05:06,475 --> 00:05:10,597
The line of best fit is y equals negative
one point five x plus one hundred

112
00:05:10,617 --> 00:05:11,323
forty.

113
00:05:11,343 --> 00:05:13,893
On the day with a high
temperature of forty degrees,

114
00:05:13,913 --> 00:05:16,914
the cart sold ninety-five hot drinks.

115
00:05:16,986 --> 00:05:20,750
How many more hot drinks did the cart
sell that day than the number predicted by

116
00:05:20,770 --> 00:05:22,303
the line of best fit?

117
00:05:22,323 --> 00:05:23,537
Pause and try it.

118
00:05:26,787 --> 00:05:28,981
Find the predicted value first.

119
00:05:29,001 --> 00:05:31,037
Plug forty into the line.

120
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:35,053
Negative one point five times
forty is negative sixty,

121
00:05:35,073 --> 00:05:37,357
plus one hundred forty is eighty.

122
00:05:37,465 --> 00:05:39,770
The line predicts eighty drinks.

123
00:05:39,790 --> 00:05:41,876
The actual number was ninety-five.

124
00:05:41,896 --> 00:05:45,484
Ninety-five minus eighty is
fifteen, so the answer is fifteen.

125
00:05:45,504 --> 00:05:49,076
On the graph, that's the vertical
gap from the line up to the dot.

126
00:05:49,114 --> 00:05:51,487
The traps are eighty, the predicted value,

127
00:05:51,507 --> 00:05:54,221
and ninety-five, the actual value.

128
00:05:54,435 --> 00:05:56,236
The question asks for the difference,

129
00:05:56,256 --> 00:05:57,293
so you need both.

130
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,269
Question four.

131
00:05:58,289 --> 00:06:01,304
A student recorded the area,
y, in square centimeters,

132
00:06:01,324 --> 00:06:05,645
covered by a mold colony x days
after it was first observed.

133
00:06:05,789 --> 00:06:09,554
For days zero through six,
the areas were two point one,

134
00:06:09,574 --> 00:06:12,483
two point seven, four
point oh, five point six,

135
00:06:12,503 --> 00:06:16,181
seven point five, eleven point
oh, and fourteen point eight.

136
00:06:16,271 --> 00:06:18,664
Which equation best models the data?

137
00:06:18,696 --> 00:06:19,910
Pause and try it.

138
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,283
Check the pattern.

139
00:06:25,303 --> 00:06:27,819
The differences grow: zero point six,

140
00:06:27,839 --> 00:06:30,390
then one point three, and
up to three point eight.

141
00:06:30,410 --> 00:06:31,909
So it isn't linear.

142
00:06:32,266 --> 00:06:33,533
Now the ratios.

143
00:06:33,553 --> 00:06:36,925
Each value is about one point
four times the one before.

144
00:06:36,945 --> 00:06:39,482
A steady multiplier means exponential.

145
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:42,861
An exponential model looks
like a times b to the x.

146
00:06:42,881 --> 00:06:46,290
The starting value, a, is
about two, and the multiplier,

147
00:06:46,310 --> 00:06:48,290
b, is about one point four.

148
00:06:48,310 --> 00:06:51,897
That's y equals two times
one point four to the x.

149
00:06:51,917 --> 00:06:53,808
The answer is D.

150
00:06:53,828 --> 00:06:56,307
A has a base less than one, so it shrinks.

151
00:06:56,327 --> 00:06:57,487
That's decay.

152
00:06:57,507 --> 00:07:01,165
C swaps a and b, and it's
way too big by day six.

153
00:07:01,185 --> 00:07:02,630
And B is a line.

154
00:07:02,650 --> 00:07:05,273
It's close to the best
line through these points,

155
00:07:05,293 --> 00:07:07,364
but a line can't follow the curve.

156
00:07:07,429 --> 00:07:10,873
In Desmos, enter the table,
then graph each choice.

157
00:07:10,893 --> 00:07:14,251
Only D follows the points
all the way across.

158
00:07:14,305 --> 00:07:16,483
Three traps before the harder questions.

159
00:07:16,590 --> 00:07:18,820
One: the model is not exact.

160
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:23,590
Words like always, every, and
exactly don't belong with a trend.

161
00:07:23,697 --> 00:07:27,962
Two: slope is the change
in y per one unit of x,

162
00:07:27,982 --> 00:07:29,573
never the other way around.

163
00:07:29,593 --> 00:07:31,894
Three: predicted versus actual.

164
00:07:31,914 --> 00:07:33,751
The line gives the predicted value.

165
00:07:33,771 --> 00:07:35,878
The dot gives the actual value.

166
00:07:35,986 --> 00:07:38,572
Before you answer, ask which
one the question wants,

167
00:07:38,592 --> 00:07:40,627
or whether it wants the gap between them.

168
00:07:40,648 --> 00:07:41,700
Question five.

169
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:45,235
The scatterplot shows
the age, x, in years,

170
00:07:45,255 --> 00:07:50,183
and the height, y, in meters, of
twelve trees of one species in a park.

171
00:07:50,327 --> 00:07:54,878
The line of best fit is y equals zero
point six x plus one point eight.

172
00:07:54,898 --> 00:07:59,299
Which statement is best supported by the
scatterplot and the line of best fit?

173
00:07:59,319 --> 00:08:00,264
Pause and try it.

174
00:08:00,284 --> 00:08:01,784
Take a little longer on this one.

175
00:08:05,976 --> 00:08:08,225
Test each statement against the data.

176
00:08:08,369 --> 00:08:12,884
A says the line predicts seven point
two meters for a nine-year-old tree.

177
00:08:12,904 --> 00:08:15,956
Zero point six times
nine is five point four,

178
00:08:15,976 --> 00:08:18,313
plus one point eight is seven point two.

179
00:08:18,333 --> 00:08:20,547
And nine is inside the data.

180
00:08:20,690 --> 00:08:21,671
That works.

181
00:08:21,691 --> 00:08:26,584
B says the nine-year-old tree in the
sample is seven point two meters tall.

182
00:08:26,906 --> 00:08:28,707
But that's the predicted value.

183
00:08:28,727 --> 00:08:31,350
The actual dot is at six point five.

184
00:08:31,370 --> 00:08:34,313
C says the older tree is always taller,

185
00:08:34,333 --> 00:08:37,227
but the nine-year-old is
shorter than the eight-year-old.

186
00:08:37,318 --> 00:08:40,761
And D uses the line for
an eighty-year-old tree.

187
00:08:40,781 --> 00:08:44,369
That's far outside ages two to fourteen,

188
00:08:44,389 --> 00:08:47,583
and trees don't keep growing
at the same rate forever.

189
00:08:47,603 --> 00:08:49,797
That prediction isn't reliable.

190
00:08:49,817 --> 00:08:51,385
The answer is A.

191
00:08:51,405 --> 00:08:53,119
Last one, the hardest.

192
00:08:53,154 --> 00:08:56,527
The scatterplot shows
the depth, x, in meters,

193
00:08:56,547 --> 00:08:59,419
below the surface of a lake,
and the water temperature,

194
00:08:59,439 --> 00:09:02,297
y, in degrees Celsius, at twelve depths.

195
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:06,179
A line of best fit is shown,
but its equation isn't given.

196
00:09:06,199 --> 00:09:09,465
For the measurement at a
depth of fifteen meters,

197
00:09:09,485 --> 00:09:14,679
what is the actual temperature minus
the temperature predicted by the line of

198
00:09:14,699 --> 00:09:16,913
best fit, in degrees Celsius?

199
00:09:16,972 --> 00:09:17,916
Pause and try it.

200
00:09:17,936 --> 00:09:19,436
Take a little longer on this one.

201
00:09:23,628 --> 00:09:26,036
No equation, so build one from the graph.

202
00:09:26,056 --> 00:09:29,537
Find two points where the line
crosses grid intersections:

203
00:09:29,557 --> 00:09:32,501
zero, twenty-four, and twenty, eight.

204
00:09:32,521 --> 00:09:34,607
The slope is eight minus twenty-four,

205
00:09:34,627 --> 00:09:37,699
over twenty, which is
negative zero point eight.

206
00:09:37,950 --> 00:09:39,985
The y intercept is twenty-four.

207
00:09:40,109 --> 00:09:44,375
At a depth of fifteen, the line predicts
negative twelve plus twenty-four,

208
00:09:44,395 --> 00:09:46,109
which is twelve degrees.

209
00:09:46,430 --> 00:09:50,180
The actual dot at fifteen
sits at ten degrees.

210
00:09:50,221 --> 00:09:52,844
Actual minus predicted
is ten minus twelve,

211
00:09:52,864 --> 00:09:54,415
which is negative two.

212
00:09:54,435 --> 00:09:57,665
The dot is below the line, so
the answer has to be negative.

213
00:09:57,685 --> 00:10:01,381
If you got positive two, you
subtracted in the wrong order.

214
00:10:01,401 --> 00:10:03,222
Here's the method for test day.

215
00:10:03,329 --> 00:10:07,722
Step one: read the axes and
the units before anything else.

216
00:10:07,758 --> 00:10:10,059
Step two: name the question type.

217
00:10:10,079 --> 00:10:14,559
Association, interpretation,
predicted versus actual,

218
00:10:14,579 --> 00:10:17,401
choosing a model, or which
statement is supported.

219
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:21,349
Step three: for any prediction,
plug x into the line,

220
00:10:21,369 --> 00:10:24,012
and check that x is inside the data.

221
00:10:24,369 --> 00:10:26,920
Step four: when they ask what's supported,

222
00:10:26,940 --> 00:10:29,598
test every statement
against the actual dots,

223
00:10:29,618 --> 00:10:32,262
and be wary of absolute words.

224
00:10:32,291 --> 00:10:34,377
Use Desmos when the choices are models,

225
00:10:34,397 --> 00:10:36,005
or there's no equation.

226
00:10:36,113 --> 00:10:39,093
Enter the points in a table,
then graph each choice,

227
00:10:39,113 --> 00:10:42,520
or type y one, tilde, m x one plus b,

228
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:44,077
to get a line of best fit.

229
00:10:44,148 --> 00:10:46,541
For a quick prediction,
just plug in by hand.

230
00:10:46,562 --> 00:10:48,276
That's scatterplots.

231
00:10:48,812 --> 00:10:51,614
Associations are trends,
the line predicts,

232
00:10:51,634 --> 00:10:55,792
the dots are actual, and predictions
get risky outside the data.

233
00:10:55,812 --> 00:11:00,513
For official practice, filter the free
Question Bank by two-variable data.

234
00:11:00,533 --> 00:11:04,012
Every question and data set in this
video was made up for practice,

235
00:11:04,032 --> 00:11:06,354
in the style of the real test.

236
00:11:06,462 --> 00:11:10,727
Next up: SAT nonlinear
equations and systems.

237
00:11:10,747 --> 00:11:13,104
If this helped, subscribe so you catch it.
